// 0.179.52 (13/11): **the card of the system has a way back, at the left of the way out**. The owner: *«Afegir botó de "back" al
// panell lliscant de la barra de sistema. Per tirar l'app a la vista anterior. A la part esquerra del panell, a la dreta el "close"
// com fins ara. El back ha de ser una icona, com el close»* (docs/30, docs/50):
//   - **la fletxa és el mateix botó que la creu, a l'altra cantonada**: sixty-four pixels a side, the same twenty-four from the top of
//     the card and the same twenty-four from the edge, painted by the same `ui::paint_a_button` every button of this tree is painted
//     with —the face of paper lifted four pixels, the ink under it, the frame on the face and the word in the middle—, so the card
//     reads as two keys of one system and not as two drawings (`back_x` is `kBackLeft` plus half a side, `paint_the_button` takes the
//     word and the step now that there are two of them);
//   - **la icona és una fletxa i no un dibuix de píxels**: `0x81`, the one byte CP1252 leaves empty and that the face answers with
//     `U+2190` (0.158.0), at three steps and not four: an arrow is wider than an `X` and at four the frame of the control cuts it. A
//     word would be the word of a language and an arrow is not. **One byte and not three**: a text here is one byte a character, and
//     the UTF-8 `←` was three characters on the glass —`â†↓`, which is how the first drawing of this button was found—;
//   - **el toc no inventa cap camí**: it asks `shell::go_back_one_view`, the door the pinch from big to small already uses, so the app
//     gives its top view back, hears `on_back(depth)` and repaints the page below it. The card drops the hold of the page **without a
//     paint**, says the system owes the page whole (`ui::owe_the_page()`), and the `present` the app makes inside its own `on_back` is
//     the one wash that erases the card —one pass of this glass for one finger and not two, which is the same rule the close follows
//     when a page goes back (0.179.23)—;
//   - **i amb una sola pàgina la fletxa no hi és**: an app that never pushed a view has nowhere to go back to, and a button that cannot
//     do anything is worse than no button —the rule the cross has followed over a launcher since 0.179.25—. It asks `apps::views()`
//     before painting, so the corner of the card of a one-page app is paper and a tap there is a tap on the card;
//   - **mesurat**: `test_the_arrow_of_the_panel_goes_back_one_view` (test_apps) runs an app that pushes a view, pulls the card down from
//     the bar, reads the three things that make the arrow a key of this system at the glass —the ink of the shadow, the paper of the
//     face off the arrow and the ink of the arrow in the middle—, taps its middle and reads the view count going from one to zero, the
//     `stacky back 0` of the hook and the whole page washed with `gc16`; then pulls the card again over the same app, now with no view,
//     and reads paper where the key was, no arrow in it, the app still there and the count still zero. **The case is red without the
//     one byte** —it was checked by putting the UTF-8 word back, which draws `â†↓` and fails the «wider than tall» reading with
//     `-82`— and the case of the cross still passes beside it; **the whole suite was not run again after that**, because the owner
//     stopped the runs, so `619 cases` is the count of the run before the last two lines of this note; the five boards and the
//     emulator are built. **I la suite que va venir la va trobar vermella**: el cas era verd tot sol i vermell a la suite, i el
//     forat que va obrir —una pàgina que el sistema deu i que no té cap regió marcada— és el que tanca la 0.179.53.

// 0.179.51 (13/11): **a page of a list is turned with a finger that goes up, and the shelf of the faces has a card**. The
// owner: *«L'app fonts no passa pàgina de la llista amb swipe, usa el paginador Dots intern de la llista o afegit manualment? En
// cas de ser intern, el control registra bé els swipe?»* (docs/30, docs/40, docs/90):
//   - **el paginador és intern i el control registrava el gest a mitges**: the dots of the foot are the list's own (0.174.2) and
//     since 0.179.4 the control turns its page with a finger — but the travel it measured was **sideways only**, so a hand that
//     goes **up or down** over a page that never scrolls did nothing, and that is the gesture a person makes on the shelf of the
//     faces. Left and up are the page after this one, right and down the one before, and the axis the finger walked most is the
//     one that says which. A list and a grid both, because both are pages and neither has a scroll to give the vertical its other
//     meaning (`kPageSwipeSlop`, the landing's `y` is kept now the way its `x` already was);
//   - **and el que no canvia és la regla de l'amo**: the gesture is the control's when it **begins** on it —a swipe that starts on
//     a row turns the page even if the finger ends outside the list—, a contact that walked twenty pixels is never a press (0.179.29)
//     so a swipe picks no row, and **a point that is not on a row is not a stop of anything**: a finger that lands on the foot with
//     the dots or in the margin of the box is on no control and turns nothing. That last one is the hole this version leaves
//     written down and does not close (the foot is thirty-seven rows of a list that are the paginator's and not a target);
//   - **i la lleixa diu en quina pàgina és** (`fonts: page 2`): the app did not have `on_page`, so a page turned by a finger left
//     no line in the log and a test could only see the ink;
//   - **i l'app de les cares té targeta** (0.179.51): `fonts` reads the whole directory of `/fonts` and opens one face of each of
//     the four formats, which is files of the disk before its first page —`tools/app_splash.py --icon
//     apps/fonts/res/icon-source.png --title Fonts --foot lunokOS`, **209 × 447 i 5 276 B** from the 448 master, the recipe of the
//     launcher's card and not a page of the glass— and `"splash"` in its manifest (app 0.2.0);
//   - **mesurat**: two cases. `test_a_swipe_up_turns_the_page_of_a_list` (test_apps) writes twenty files into `res/fonts` —which
//     `/fonts` presents as a directory— runs the app, swipes up from the first row and reads `fonts: page 2` with **no row picked**,
//     then swipes down and reads `page 1`; and the case of the grid grows the same half (a finger up over a cell turns to the second
//     page and the ring lands on its first cell). **The case of the list is red without this version's line** —it was checked by
//     turning the vertical travel off and running it— and the whole suite is green (`618 cases`, 24 suites), with the five boards and
//     the emulator built.

// 0.179.50 (13/11): **the page of the hour shows the hour of summer and not the leap day**. The owner, with the page of the time
// zone on the emulator: *«A l'app Time zone surt "Leap year" i aquesta dada no es important, l'important es el "Daylight time"
// (horari d'estiu!)»* (docs/30, docs/60):
//   - **la casella és `Daylight time` i suma una hora a la zona**: checked, the offset of the map goes sixty minutes east —in the
//     band that is filled, in the words `Selected timezone: +01:00` and in the number the close saves—. It is a **shift of this
//     page** and not a second setting, because the board keeps one number: a board that reads +02:00 in July and +01:00 in
//     December keeps the same setting all year, and a country that shifts by half an hour is a `time.tz` of its own
//     (`kDaylightMinutes`, `shown_offset` and `shown_hour` in `apps/tz/tz.lua`);
//   - **i el dia de traspàs surt de la pàgina sense perdre's**: it is still a setting of the board —`cfg leap`, `time.leap`, and
//     the clock that comes from a server turns it on, which is the rule of 9/11— and it keeps its two homes; what it does not have
//     any more is a box on the page of the hour, which is what the owner asked for (docs/60);
//   - **i la pàgina que s'esborra demana els seus controls**: `ui.clear` covers what the children of the page had drawn and a
//     control draws only when it is marked, so a page painted whole after the box —or after a sync, which had the fault since
//     0.174.0— left the button and the list white until the next finger. `paint_page` invalidates the three of them, and
//     `invalidate` of a parent asks its children (the rule of 0.168.4) (found in the window, 13/11);
//   - **mesurat**: the case of the page walks its three controls with the dial as before, and now the second one is the box of the
//     hour of summer: the centre turns it on (`tz: dst on +01:00`, and the leap day of the board is **not** turned), the finger
//     turns it off (`tz: dst off +03:00`), it is turned on again and the close saves **+04:00** (`cfg tz` says the same). En la
//     finestra: la casella surt a la pàgina, la banda i la frase es mouen una hora i el botó i el desplegable hi són després del
//     canvi. `617 cases` i la suite sencera verda, les cinc plaques i l'emulador construïts.

